<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Hold</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>hold &lt;item&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>hold wand
wield sword
hold dagger
</pre>
<p>Lets you hold an item in your hand. To use a wand or a staff, for example, you 
must hold it (see <a cmd='#'>Help Use</a>).
</p><p>You can hold an item in one hand and wield a one-handed weapon in the other. You 
can also fight with two one-handed weapons, by wielding one and holding the 
other: then your attacks take turns with the two, and the skill two weapon style 
makes you better at it. Some weapons are too large to be the second one, and a 
two-handed weapon needs both hands free.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Wield</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Use</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Two Weapon Style</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Wands</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Staves</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Remove</a>
</pre>




</div>